      "text": "For seven years, Christmas will occur on Saturday, December 26. On four of those years, the week inclusive of the New Year will also include a holiday. In these years, January 24 will also be a Sunday.\n\nFor the remaining three years, the New Year will not occur on a holiday within the week, so January 24 will not be a Sunday. In either case, in seven years, the week of December 23 will end on a Sunday.\n\nTo find December 23, we need to subtract five days from Sunday, giving December 23 on a Wednesday. \nAnswer: \\boxed{Wednesday}.\nNo explanation was provided. How can you possibly know that they are seven years? The statement starts with the statement that if Thanksgiving is on Thursday, then 20 numbers later, Christmas will be on Saturday.\n\nA simple approach to approach these type problems is to say that on Thanksgiving 2020, Christmas would be on Monday, December 26.\n\nIf we mark all days of all of these 7 consecutive years, we will end up having 7 Mondays.\n\nIf we draw grid of 5th years, answering will surely be obvious - Wednesday as it only has 5 Mondays within the year.",
