      "text": "For later reference, let's write a Python script to help us with the day-of-the-week calculations.\n#### Step 1: Determine the day of the week for November 23.\n- The problem states that Thanksgiving falls on Thursday, November 23$^{\\circ}$.\n- Now we will determine the day of the week for November 23 using the date arithmetic code.\n  \n- This significant in order to have an effective difference for December 23$^{\\circ}$ calculation and per from th coming question stage to come.\n  \n```\nimport datetime\n# Define the dates\nthanksgiving_date = datetime.datetime(2023, 11, 23)  # Thanksgiving occurs on the 23rd of November\ndecember_23rd_date = datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 23) # December 23rd falls 79 days after Thanksgiving\n\n# Calculate the difference in days\ndifference = (december_23rd_date - thanksgiving_date).days\n\n# Combine the findings where th this function orders dates on a 7-(day of the week pattern)\nweekdays = [\"Monday\", \"Tuesday\", \"Wednesday\", \"Thursday\", \"Friday\", \"Saturday\", \"Sunday\"]\nday_of_week = weekdays[difference % 7]\n\n# Print the day of week\nprint(day_of_week)\n```\n#### Step 2: The day of the week for December 23 in 2023 falls on \\(\\boxed{\\text{Thursday}}\\).",
