      "text": "December 23 is the 31st of the 11th month. Since November is in the 11th month of the calendar, we can figure out what day of the week it is on November 23 according to the calendar system. To do so, we also need to know what day of the week it is in October. We can use Thursday, November 23, as a reference, which means:\n\n- October has 31 days. \n- November has 30 days. \n- November 23, 2020, is Thursday in October\n\nOctober 31, 2020, will be Friday. The next day will be October 31, 2020, which indicates that October 31 is Friday, October 31, 2020. We then need to find what day of the week it is on November 22, which is a 22-day month. Using this information, we find the day of the week on November 23 using the following calculation: \n\nFrom 22 days, we need to subtract 9, since there are exactly 7 days in a week. 10-9 = 1, to get to the first day of the next week. This means November 23 is a Thursday. December 1 and 2 are Sunday and Monday, respectively. October 30, 2020, comes before October 31.\n\nThe next day after October 31 is Friday. The following day is Saturday. Hence, December 1 is a Saturday, December 2 is a Sunday, and December 23 is a Monday. Therefore, December 23 occurs on a Tuesday in 2020, which means the answer is Tuesday.",
